course: dictionary
lesson: 2065
title: Consistent: the same every time
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Consistent means behaving or happening in the same way every time, so you can rely on it. Look at the clues around the word. «Both single ('...') and double ("...") inverted commas are correct; many UK books use single and US books double; be consistent.» The sentence tells you what to do: choose one style and use it the same way all the way through.
explain: Now read the second example: «Both James's book and James' book are used; style guides differ, and what matters is being consistent.» Both forms are allowed, so consistent cannot mean "correct" here. It means keeping to one choice without switching. Swap in "the same every time" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In science, consistent means the same result each time you repeat a test. If your results jump all over the place, they are not consistent. Watch for the phrase "consistent with", which means in agreement with something, like a witness whose story matches the facts.
fact: Consistent means always behaving or happening in the same way, steady and reliable.
fact: «Consistent with» means in agreement with something, so it does not contradict it.
fact: In science, results are consistent when repeating a test gives the same or very close answer.
fact: In sport, «a consistent player» plays well every time, not just once in a while.
fact: «Be consistent» means keep to one choice the same way all the way through, such as one style of inverted commas.
exercise: «In science experiments, results should be consistent when you repeat them.» What does consistent mean here? | *The same or very close each time you test | Written down neatly | Different every time you test | Done by a grown-up only
exercise: «In sport a consistent player plays well every time.» What does consistent suggest about the player? | Plays badly most days | Lucky once in a while | Tall and fast | *Steady and reliable, playing well every time
exercise: Ella says «be consistent» means change your style often. What does it really mean? | Never use any style at all | Change your style on every page | Ask a friend what to choose | *Keep to one choice the same way all the way through
test: «Both James's book and James' book are used; what matters is being consistent.» Which word is closest in meaning to consistent here? | Lost | Late | Angry | *Keeping to the same choice throughout
test: «A witness's account should be consistent with the facts.» What does consistent with mean? | *In agreement with the facts | Different from the facts, on purpose | Against the law | Louder than the facts
exam: Mia's quiz scores are 8, 8, 9 and 8 out of 10 each time she takes the quiz. Which word best describes her scores? | Furious | Lucky | Random | *Consistent
